---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { entity } from "../data/entity";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Income and Results Disclaimer"
  description="No income promises appear anywhere on this site. Read exactly what our results claims mean, and what our guarantee actually covers."
>
  <section class="bg-navy-900 text-offwhite-100">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-16">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-4">LEGAL</p>
      <h1 class="on-navy">Disclaimer</h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-ivory-50">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-14 leading-relaxed">
      <div class="card p-5 border-dashed bg-gold-100 border-gold-500 mb-10">
        <p class="font-semibold">
          This is a draft starting point. Have a lawyer review this page before it governs real
          transactions. [NEEDS CONFIRMATION: legal review]
        </p>
      </div>

      <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 mb-8">Last updated: [NEEDS CONFIRMATION: publish date]</p>

      <h2>No income promises, anywhere on this site</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">
        Nothing on this website, in a call, in an email, or in any of our marketing promises you income,
        sales, or any specific financial result. Writing and publishing a book with us does not guarantee
        you'll earn money from it, land a client, or book a stage. We say this plainly because it's true, and
        because we'd rather lose a sale than make a promise we can't keep.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10">What our numbers actually mean</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">
        You'll see real numbers on this site: {entity.proofBank.authorsCount} authors across
        {entity.proofBank.countriesCount} countries, {entity.proofBank.fastSaleStat.toLowerCase()}, and
        {entity.proofBank.rescueStat.toLowerCase()}. These describe things that happened, for us and for
        specific clients. They are not an average, a typical result, or a forecast for what will happen for
        you.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 font-semibold">
        {entity.incomeDisclaimerLine}
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4">
        Every place on this site where a result, a number, or a revenue example appears, this same line
        applies, whether or not that page links back here directly.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10">The only guarantee that exists</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">
        We do not offer a general "guaranteed bestseller" or any blanket guarantee of book performance,
        anywhere, ever. The only guarantee that applies to any engagement is the specific, scoped guarantee
        written out in plain language on that particular service's own page and in your signed agreement.
        Read that page's guarantee section carefully, ask us to explain exactly what it covers and doesn't
        cover, and treat anything broader than what's written there as not part of our offer.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10">Testimonials and case studies</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">
        Every testimonial or case study on this site is either a real quote from a real author who gave us
        explicit permission to share it, or it is marked with a clear pending-permission placeholder (for
        example, <code>[TESTIMONIAL: pending permission]</code> or <code>[CASE STUDY: pending permission]</code>)
        until that permission exists. We do not invent authors, quotes, or numbers to fill empty space. See
        our <a href="/case-studies" class="underline font-semibold">case studies page</a> and
        <a href="/reviews" class="underline font-semibold">reviews page</a> for the current state of both.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10">Urgency and countdown timers</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">
        Any countdown timer or enrollment deadline on this site counts down to a real, dated event: an
        actual cohort start date, an actual enrollment close, or an actual bonus expiration. We do not use
        evergreen timers that reset for each visitor, and we do not invent scarcity that isn't real.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10">Questions about a specific claim</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">
        If you see a claim anywhere on this site that seems to promise a specific result, tell us. Contact
        us at {entity.contactEmail || "[NEEDS CONFIRMATION: legal contact email]"} or through our
        <a href="/contact" class="underline font-semibold">contact page</a>, and we'll fix it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
